WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:05.960
"Friends" fans around the world were devastated&nbsp;
when Matthew Perry died at the age of 54 — as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:10.800
were his fellow co-stars. Now, following&nbsp;
a heartfelt group statement from the cast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.880
Matt LeBlanc has penned his&nbsp;
own tear-jerking goodbye.

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:17.720
LeBlanc, who starred as Chandler&nbsp;
Bing's goofy roommate Joey Tribbiani,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:20.200
wrote in an emotional Instagram post:

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:24.440
"Matthew. It is with a heavy heart I say&nbsp;
goodbye. The times we had together are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:28.560
honestly among the favorite times of my&nbsp;
life. It was an honor to share the stage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:32.840
with you and to call you my friend. I will&nbsp;
always smile when I think of you and I'll&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:39.200
never forget you. Never. Spread your wings and&nbsp;
fly brother you're finally free. Much love."

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:42.760
Fittingly, LeBlanc ended his&nbsp;
tribute with a joke by saying:

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:45.440
"And I guess you're keeping&nbsp;
the 20 bucks you owe me."

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:49.480
In addition to his emotional words, which&nbsp;
reflect on their enduring friendship,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:52.600
LeBlanc shared several stills&nbsp;
of Joey and Chandler together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:56.640
highlighting just how hilarious — and&nbsp;
adorable — the duo were on "Friends."

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:01.400
Honestly, it's hard to imagine a more memorable&nbsp;
sitcom duo. The true definition of "opposites&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:05.280
attract," the lovable goofballs were&nbsp;
frequently at odds with one another,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:09.920
though they never shied away from mutual&nbsp;
admiration. Their various escapades and side&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:14.600
quests led to some of the most memorable plotlines&nbsp;
in "Friends," such as the time they adopted a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:20.960
chick and a duck. And who can forget their&nbsp;
hilarious banter in London during Ross' wedding?

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:26.960
"You're different here too!&nbsp;
You're mean in England!"

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:32.200
To this day, the duo's bromance stands out as&nbsp;
a major highlight of the show. Unsurprisingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:36.680
LeBlanc and Perry carried their on-screen&nbsp;
relationship outside of the show's bustling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:41.880
set. Back in 2015, while speaking with the&nbsp;
Television Critics Association Press Tour,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:44.840
LeBlanc gushed over his co-star. He said:

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:48.040
"I love that guy. I can not see him&nbsp;
for five years and then get in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:52.400
room together and still have a shorthand&nbsp;
with each other. It's amazing, really."

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:57.120
While LeBlanc and Perry were both quite private,&nbsp;
they were occasionally seen together. One of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:01.160
duo's most heartfelt crossovers was when&nbsp;
LeBlanc showed up to support Perry for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:06.760
his debut play "The End of Longing" back in&nbsp;
2016. LeBlanc shared in an Instagram post:

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:09.640
"He and the cast were great. Way to go bro."

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:12.320
Clearly, the two genuinely cared about each other.

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:17.280
As of this video, LeBlanc's Instagram post is&nbsp;
the first major solo statement released from a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:21.480
"Friends" cast member following Perry's&nbsp;
death. While the core cast of "Friends"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:26.520
was no doubt close — as evidenced by the&nbsp;
2021 MAX reunion special — Matthew Perry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:32.501
wished that he could see his former co-stars&nbsp;
more often. He told Access Hollywood in 2022:

00:02:32.501 --> 00:02:37.221
"We don't see each other as much. I wish&nbsp;
the group would see each other more."

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:41.640
Perry has always been candid and honest&nbsp;
about his relationship with his co-stars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:44.200
frequently praising them at every opportunity.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:49.160
In his 2022 memoir "Friends, Lovers and&nbsp;
the Big Terrible Thing," Perry opened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:53.960
up about his brutal history with addiction.&nbsp;
In an excerpt released by The Sunday Times,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:58.040
Perry discussed how LeBlanc helped&nbsp;
him stay awake on set. He wrote:

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:02.520
"But still, the addiction ravaged me — one time,&nbsp;
in a scene in the coffeehouse when I'm dressed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:07.720
in a suit, I fell asleep right there on the&nbsp;
couch, and disaster was averted only when Matt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:13.240
LeBlanc nudged me awake right before my line;&nbsp;
no one noticed, but I knew how close I'd come."

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:17.600
In the same excerpt, Perry revealed how&nbsp;
Jennifer Anniston once confronted him regarding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:22.760
his addiction, describing the encounter as&nbsp;
"devastating." While they continue to be private&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:27.720
about their personal lives, it's obvious that&nbsp;
the "Friends" cast deeply care for one another.

